0000word/settings.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000��92\u0005\u0002\u0000\u00008\u0016\u0000\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�G\u0000\u0000word/webSettings.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u00003��VE\n\u0000\u0000�]\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u001bJ\u0000\u0000word/styles.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000��\u001d�|\u0002\u0000\u00006\u000b\u0000\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�T\u0000\u0000word/fontTable.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000�\u000e���\u0001\u0000\u00000\u0003\u0000\u0000\u0011\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00009W\u0000\u0000docProps/core.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000a��#�\u000e\u0000\u0000Q\u0019\u0001\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0006Z\u0000\u0000word/numbering.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000\u0001�Ā�\u0001\u0000\u0000�\u0003\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�h\u0000\u0000docProps/app.xmlPK\u0005\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0011\u0000\u0011\u0000:\u0004\u0000\u0000�k\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000","minutes_text":"PERMITS AND LICENSES COMMITTEE\n  MINUTES\n  January 24, 2019\n\nA meeting of the Permits and License Committee was held on Thursday, January 24,\n2019, at 2:00 pm in the City Council Community Room A, 1st Floor\n\nRoll Call:  Members Present:  Harjinder Singh, Administration\n  Yvonne Horton, City Clerk – 2:06 pm\n  Cpt. Reggie Johnson, LACO Fire Department\n  Sgt. Luis Jaramillo, Police Department\n  Marissa Fewell, Planning & Building Department\n\n  Staff Present:  Peggy L. Velasquez, Finance Department\n  Serena Martinez, Finance Department\n\nAlso present: Teresa Estrada-Quintanar, Superintendent, Parks, and Recreation &\n  Community Services\n\nPublic Comments Regarding Agenda Items\nDuring public comments any person may address the Permits & License Committee,\nprovided the item is within the subject matter jurisdiction of the Permits & License\nCommittee.\nChairman Singh asked if there were any persons present who wished to address the\nPermits & License Committee on any item on the Agenda.\nChairman Singh reported that there were no public requests to speak.\n\nA motion was moved and seconded to hold-over the minutes from the meeting held on\nJanuary 10, 2019.\n\nItem #1:  A motion was moved and seconded to APPROVE the permit request for\n  Tiayana C. Walker; dba: Walker Family Events to host Inglewood Festival\n  of the Arts at Edward Vincent Jr. Park, September 7, 2019 from 10:00 am\n  – 10:00 pm, subject to contacting Los Angeles County Fire Department to\n  coordinate emergency medical services, obtain tent and/or special event\n  permits; mobile command post to manage this large-scale event and\n  deployment of one (1) Lieutenant (event commander), two (2) Sergeants\n  (supervisors) and fourteen (14) officers (2-4 of the 14 officers will be bicycle\n  officers and six (6) Traffic Control Officer’s from 0830-2300 (14.5 hours); if\n  serving and/or selling alcoholic beverages the event organization is\n  responsible for ensuring vendors and/or caterers hold a current and valid\n  Alcohol Beverage Control license; designate a controlled area for the\n  service and/or sales of alcohol; 4-5 professional licensed security guards\n  are required to be assigned to each alcohol service area to manage crowd\n  control, check for proper identification to prevent underage drinking and\n  maintain safety of attendees throughout the duration of the event; payment\n  of invoice for city staffing and services is due, Wednesday, August 7, 2019;\n  finalized list of site plan with measurements; vendors, guest speakers,\n  entertainment, performing artists, dignitaries and event activities due to the\n  Finance Department, Thursday, June 6, 2019; provide adequate parking\n  for patrons; maintain event site, ensuring no littering and loitering; maintain\n\fPermits & License Committee  January 24, 2019\nMinutes  Page 2 of 5\n\n  site at all times ensuring site is properly cleaned immediately at the end of\n  the event; ensure safe pedestrian and vehicular circulation on/off site;\n  adhere to all applicable IMC regulations, including noise and signage.\n  Motion carried unanimously. (Activity No. 00272898)\n\nItem #2:  A motion was moved and seconded to APPROVE the permit request for\n  Northgate Market to conduct a Valentine’s Day parking lot sale at 10801 S.\n  Prairie Ave., February 13-14, 2019 from 7:00 am – 7:00 pm, subject to\n  hiring three (3) licensed security guards from a professional security guard\n  service company that is also licensed with the City of Inglewood to maintain\n  and manage crowd control, ensuring safe accessibility to grocery store\n  aisles; assign one (1) security guard to maintain traffic control in the parking\n  lot; any person directing traffic must wear highly-visible, retro-reflective\n  vests; maintain site at all times, ensure site is properly cleaned immediately\n  at the end of the parking lot sale; merchandise display is only permitted,\n  February 13-14, 2019; emergency exits/access and all walkways cannot\n  be obstructed; outdoor merchandise cannot obstruct designated white,\n  yellow, blue or red parking zones; comply with Inglewood Municipal Code\n  Noise Regulations (reference Section 5-28. Noise Level Measurement and\n  Section 5-30. Maximum Residential Noise Levels); ensure safe pedestrian\n  and vehicular circulation on/off site; adhere to all applicable IMC\n  regulations, including noise and signage. Motion carried unanimously.\n  (Activity No. 00273288)\n\nItem #3:  A motion was moved and seconded to APPROVE the permit request for Girl\n  Scouts of Greater Los Angeles to conduct their annual cookie sale at various\n  retail locations throughout the City, January 27 through March 11, 2019,\n  subject to all girl scouts must be accompanied by adult supervision, wear their\n  uniforms, badge and proper girl scout identification; sales conducted at retail\n  store fronts must be with the permission of store management; adhere to all\n  applicable IMC regulations, including noise and signage. Motion carried\n  unanimously. (Activity No. 00273299)\n\nItem #4:  A motion was moved and seconded to APPROVE the business license request\n  for Peter Burke and Rob Allen; dba: Traveller’s Autobarn to operate a\n  campervan rental at 500 W. Florence Ave., subject to payment of annual\n  business license and tax fees; Los Angeles County Fire Department field\n  inspection; an expired or lapsed license for more than six months will\n  negatively impact your license renewal; provide copy of commercial lease\n  agreement, government-issued identification for business owners and their\n  employee’s to the Finance Department; retail sales activity is strictly\n  prohibited; automobiles are not permitted to be displayed for sale, parked\n  or repaired on City streets and/or alleys; Adhere to all applicable IMC rules\n  and regulations, including noise and signage. Motion carried unanimously.\n  (Activity No. 00249419)\n\fPermits & License Committee  January 24, 2019\nMinutes  Page 3 of 5\n\nItem #5:  A motion was moved and seconded to APPROVE the business license\n  request for Christian Martin; dba: Team FM, LLC to host live entertainment\n  at 162 N. La Brea Ave., subject to payment of annual business license and\n  tax fees; Los Angeles County Fire Department field inspection; valid and\n  current Alcohol Beverage Control license; maintain records of all on-site\n  alcohol sales; comply with SP-779 (209 square feet of dance floor); comply\n  with Inglewood Municipal Code Noise Regulations; unannounced and\n  random compliance monitoring and inspections of establishment and files\n  and/or records during regular business hours; adhere to all IMC rules and\n  regulations, including noise and signage. Motion carried unanimously\n  (Activity No 00272708)\n\nItem #6:  Nooruddin Noorani; dba:  In and Out Non-Emergency Medical\n  Transportation to provide non-emergency transportation within the City,\n  Committee recommended item be held-over until all issues are addressed\n  and corrected with the Planning Department. (Activity No. 00272729)\n\nItem #7:  A motion was moved and seconded to APPROVE the business license\n  request for Tiffini Johnson and Faye B. Reid; dba: Tiffini Blue Motors to\n  operate as an Auto Broker (office use only) at 1325 N. La Brea Ave., subject\n  to payment of annual business license and tax fees; Los Angeles County\n  Fire Department field inspection; an expired or lapsed license for more than\n  six months will negatively impact your license renewal; provide copy of\n  Department of Motor Vehicles, Dealer License-Auto Broker to the Finance\n  Department; Strictly limited to office use only; Retail sales activity is strictly\n  prohibited; on-site, sales transactions must be conducted off-site, by\n  telephone, mail or electronic communication; signs advertising used auto\n  sales is not permitted on the property; automobiles are not permitted to be\n  displayed for sale, parked or repaired on City streets and/or alleys; Adhere\n  to all applicable IMC rules and regulations, including noise and signage.\n  Motion carried unanimously. (Activity No. 00272769)\n\nItem #8:  Adiam Kasmai; dba: Pure Sky Lounge to operate as a tobacco retailer and\n  hookah lounge at 630 N. La Brea Ave., Unit 105, Committee recommended\n  item be held over and scheduled on Permits & License Committee Agenda,\n  February 14, 2019. (Activity No. 00249495)\n\nItem #9:  Anisa Shah, Inc.; dba: Sharif’s Smoke Shop to operate as a tobacco\n  retailer at 151 W. Manchester Blvd., Committee recommended item be held\n  over and scheduled on Permits & License Committee Agenda, February\n  14, 2019. (Activity No. 00272723)\n\nItem #10:  A motion was moved and seconded to APPROVE the tobacco retailer\n  license request for Salah Othman; dba: Icy Mo’s Mini Mart to operate as a\n  tobacco retailer at 420 E. Florence Ave., subject to payment of annual\n  tobacco retailer license and business tax fees; sales of single cigarettes is\n  strictly prohibited; sales of tobacco, hookah, vapor and e-cigarette products\n  to minors, under age 21 is strictly prohibited; persons purchasing tobacco\n  or any related tobacco products shall have valid identification on their\n  person at all times to enforce laws restricting underage access to tobacco\n  use, including hookah products;  “NO LOITERING,” “NO\n  TRESSPASSING,” and “NO PANHANDLING” signage must be posted\n\fPermits & License Committee  January 24, 2019\nMinutes  Page 4 of 5\n\n  outside of the business; sales of marijuana and cannabis products,\n  narcotics and narcotics paraphernalia, i.e., any type of pipe used to ingest\n  other narcotics such as base “crack” cocaine, methamphetamine, including\n  glass cylindrical tube and bubble shaped pipes used to smoke and/or\n  ingest narcotics; sales of Tobacco pipes is permitted; sales or display of\n  any type of weapons, i.e., clubs, swords, knives, pepper spray, Taser/Stun\n  guns is strictly prohibited; Tobacco Retailer business owners and/or new\n  applicants or their designees is subject to random Permits & Licensing\n  establishment inspections at any time of the day or night by any Police and\n  Code Enforcement officers; purpose of random inspections is to enforce\n  business establishments adhere to the regulations set forth by the City of\n  Inglewood and for Community Public Health & Safety; parties, social events\n  or gatherings of any type is strictly prohibited; music boxes, live\n  bands/music, disc jockeys (DJ’s), etc., is strictly prohibited; business\n  owner(s) is required to operate within normal business hours; adhere to all\n  applicable IMC rules and regulations, including noise and signage. Motion\n  carried unanimously. (Activity No. 00273038)\n\nItem #11:  Following discussion, the Permits & License (P&L) Committee pulled (No.\n  26) South Park Doggie LAX and is requesting the Finance Department\n  notify the applicant in writing that his application is incomplete and needs\n  to provide a copy of his government-issued identification and verify address\n  of residency to the Finance Department. (Activity No. 00249941)\n\n  A motion was moved and seconded to collectively APPROVE the following\n  list of business license renewals (Nos. 1-25) as recommended:\n\n  Activity  Activity\n  Business Name  Business Name\n  No.  No.\n  As You Wish Non-\n  Emergency\n 1  Transportation, LLC  00249690  10  IWS Motorsport  00249723\n 2  Kumquat Holdings, LLC  00249786  11  Abrahambi, Inc.  00249717\n 3  Hernandez Ice Cream Truck  00249937  12  Lonnie's Beauty Salon  00249880\n  American Professional\n 4  Kars Co.  00249729  13  Ambulance, Inc.  00249672\n 5  Ruby Nails  00249923  14  Linda's Beauty Salon  00249814\n 6  Casa Gamino  00249955  15  Jennifer's Long Nails #1  00249816\n  Fiesta Martin Bar & Grill,\n 7  Michale Bellante  00249968  16  LLC  00249982\n 8  Contempo Nails & Spa  00249908  17  DRSS Ice Cream  00249928\n 9  Inglewood Beauty Salon  00249765  18  Lan's Nails  00249899\n\fPermits & License Committee  January 24, 2019\nMinutes  Page 5 of 5\n\n  Activity  Activity\n  Business Name  Business Name\n  No.  No.\n 19  All Town Ambulance, LLC  00249677  23  V&N Nails  00249819\n  Tricolor California Auto\n 20  Group, LLC  00249734  24  LA Auto Liquidators, Inc.  00249744\n 21  Festival Travel  00249991  25  Cathy's Nails & Spa  00249820\n 22  Captial Nails  00249826  26  South Park Doggie LAX  00249941\n\n  Subject to payment of business tax; adhere to all applicable IMC\n  regulations, including noise and signage. Motion carried unanimously.\n\nThere being no further business, the meeting was adjourned at 2:47 pm.\n\n  Respectfully submitted,\n  Peggy L. Velasquez, Recording Secretary","tries":1}